      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_8d0c001c",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: harmful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts actor Christian Bale and his wife, Sibi Blazic, posing in front of a Batmobile at what appears to be a promotional event. The overlaid text reads: 'ever notice christians are horrible drivers.' This meme uses a juxtaposition of a well-known Christian actor with a stereotype about Christians being bad drivers. The intent is to make a derogatory generalization about a religious group based on a perceived negative trait (driving ability), which is a harmful stereotype. While the meme does not target individuals by race, gender, or sexual orientation, it does target a religious group (Christians) with a negative and potentially offensive stereotype. The meme is harmful because it promotes prejudice against Christians by associating them with a negative trait, which can contribute to social division and misunderstanding. The meme does not contain abusive, cyberbullying, or propaganda elements, but it does contain a harmful stereotype that can be offensive to members of the Christian community.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_63c1a037"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
