      "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
      "label": "User projected onto the textual stereotype",
      "description": "The user is projected onto the textual material 'ever notice christians are horrible drivers', which frames the viewer as someone who is supposed to recognize or have noticed the stereotype. The meme implicitly invites the user to engage with the stereotype by making it seem like a common observation, thus projecting the user's identity onto the act of noticing or perpetuating the stereotype.",
